* In colloquial Czech, ''by'' is commonly used in place of other conditional forms of ''být'' in both singular and plural if the subject is deducible from context (from the conjugated form of the verb). That is, ''by'' is a shared clipped form of {{m|cs|bych}}, {{m|cs|bys}}, {{m|cs|bychom}} and {{m|cs|byste}}.

